[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step 06: bias control with the OSSOS ensemble
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   The standard objection to the extreme-TNO clustering is discovery
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   bias: an eccentric object is brightest near perihelion, so a survey
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   pointing at ecliptic longitude lam_d preferentially detects objects
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   whose perihelion directions lie near lam_d.  The characterized OSSOS
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   ensemble (Bannister+ 2018, ApJS 236, 18; VizieR J/ApJS/236/18) is
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   the only TNO sample with fully documented discovery circumstances --
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   per-object discovery RA/Dec, distance, magnitude, and survey block.
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   Three real-data tests on the 31 detached objects (cl='det'):
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   B1  Pointing coupling.  Circular correlation between discovery
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   ecliptic longitude lam_d and longitude of perihelion varpi.
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   Under the "found near perihelion" bias, varpi - lam_d ~ 0.
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   B2  Is OSSOS's detached sample direction different from the global
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   (SBDB) cluster axis?  OSSOS's deep blocks concentrated near
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   lam ~ 210-240 deg -- the anti-cluster side.  A uniform
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   population filtered through that footprint produces an apparent
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   concentration on the anti side: explicit demonstration of the
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   bias mechanism, and evidence the global cluster is not an
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   OSSOS artifact.
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   B3  Discovery geometry of the clustered group: were objects in the
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   clustered direction (varpi ~ 50 deg) found only by blocks
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   pointing at ~50 deg (suspicious), or across diverse pointings?
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   B4  Discovery distance: are clustered objects systematically nearer
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   perihelion at discovery (the bias channel's expected marker)?
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   Outputs: results/step_06_ossos_bias.json,
[2026-09-20 10:43:54 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 028]   figures/supplementary/step_06_ossos_bias.png
